    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4793" root="ثوأ" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَآءٌ</span></b>  <i>The name of the letter</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ث</span>, q. v.; as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَا</span>:
pl. [of the former,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَآءَاتٌ</span>; and [of the latter,]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَثْوَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَثْيَآءٌ</span>. (TA in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">باب الالف الليّنة</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It
also stands for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَنَآءٌ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَوَابٌ</span>, and the like.
(Idem ubi suprà.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  Also The <i>best</i> of anything;
as, for instance, of wheat, and of flesh-meat, and
of sugar. (Kh, TA ubi suprà.)

